Split from k238 (llm-advisor scope call). Role::Chat has no carp today when chat_f/chat_stream_realtime_f get $opts{model} != chat_model. The per-request model override only rewrites the body model field, but every model-scoped wire decision (layer 3, ADR 0023 reasoning profile, ADR 0024 exclusions, and now k238 model-scoped tool_wire_format) still keys on chat_model - so a Claude slug passed as a per-request override on a Hermes-tagged NousResearch instance would silently get the hermes prompt. Pre-existing hole, broader than k238, shippable without it. Fix: carp when the override differs from chat_model, at the chat_f/stream layer. Offline, unit-testable.

2026-09-29 20:52 Decision (when to warn). Code: a per-request model in chat_f / chat_stream_realtime_f %opts is not a canonical control, it rides %extra into chat_request/chat_stream_request and overrides the body model (OpenAI/Anthropic/Responses/Ollama dialects; Gemini + AKI route the model in the URL, see drift note). Every model-scoped decision still reads chat_model. Rule: (1) no override, undef/empty/ref, or override eq chat_model -> silent, no work. (2) Otherwise evaluate the model-scoped decisions on an in-memory clone with chat_model => override (the Manifest::Builder::_capability_clone pattern incl. _reset_derived_tool_wire_format, so ADR 0033's builder-made tag is re-resolved, a constructor tag kept) and compare with the engine as configured. (3) Only decisions THIS request consults are compared, so an override that flips nothing on the wire stays silent: capability flags (ADR 0019 layer 3 + model-aware layer 2 + ADR 0032 learned) gated per feature (tools_*/server_tools <- tools; tool_choice_* <- tool_choice; response_format_* <- response_format, json_schema also <- tool_choice (ADR 0005 rewrite); temperature <- temperature; reasoning_effort/thinking_budget <- reasoning control; parallel_tool_use <- parallel_tool_use; streaming <- stream path; image_input never, it is reporting-only per ADR 0019 k266; any other flag always, so a future model-scoped flag errs loud not silent); tool_wire_format (ADR 0033) <- tools/tool_choice; matched model_capability_exclusions rules (ADR 0024) <- tools/tool_choice/response_format; Reasoning::Profile identity (ADR 0023) <- reasoning control; _temperature_rejected_by_reasoning (ADR 0025) <- temperature; _max_tokens_key <- a length limit goes out; get_response_size (ADR 0019 k225 per-model default) <- no per-request max_tokens; _native_structured_output_for_model <- response_format. (4) Carp (not croak: the override may be intended, and Langertha does not re-scope per request -- that would need a per-request engine) naming the flipped decisions; per-request value -> every request (k247 convention), via _langertha_carp so it names the caller's line.

2026-09-29 20:56 Also found (out of scope, for the dispatcher): (a) Gemini and AKI native route the model in the URL (models/{model}:generateContent, /api/call/{model}) and ignore a per-request model for routing -- the key lands in the body as an unknown field. The k352 warning text is worded to stay true there ('model-scoped decisions follow chat_model'), but the override never reaches the provider's routing on those two engines; worth a card (croak or route it). (b) Known gap of the k352 guard: model-scoped decisions made inline rather than via a named hook are not compared, e.g. Engine::DeepSeek::reasoning_kwargs_for's _is_deepseek_v3(chat_model) thinking switch. A future named hook (or an around on _model_scoped_wire_decisions) closes it. (c) ADR: the decision 'a per-request model is not re-scoped, it is warned when it flips a consulted decision' is worth an Update on ADR 0019 (and a cross-link from 0024/0033) -- for langertha-adr-auditor, not written here.

